Error [E0749]: `protect` reaches the `IO` effect, which it prohibits with `-[!IO]>`
  --> tests/ui/crypto_expert_nonce_effect_prohibition_precedence.jet:9:21
    |
  9 | fn protect() Int -[!IO]> {
    |                     ^^
 Why: A `-[!IO]>` row means the function and every callee it can reach must not use `IO`
 Fix: Remove the call that introduces `IO`, or drop the `-[!IO]>` prohibition
